  "notes": [
    "tuning precedes Stage 0: Stage 0 runs at the tuned configs of sgd, protect and both_util, which the full run reuses; the preregistration gives Stage 0 no other source of hyperparameters",
    "within-layer means within each of the 6 weight and bias arrays",
    "ties in a trace (dead units, silent pixels) are broken at random, so every refresh of every condition has the exact same gate multiset; the gate SD check therefore cannot fail, and random tie-breaks can only lower the Spearman check",
    "the first refresh is at step 1, so a gate exists from the first update; traces update each step",
    "both_perm: P comes from the real u, exactly as in both_util; only R is the re-permuted gate, so the contrast isolates the coordination of noise with protection (Deviation 1)",
    "no bias correction or sigmoid: rank is scale-invariant, so neither can change u",
    "reuse = steps(repeat) - mean(steps(two nearest non-repeat tasks)), so lower is better; gain = -reuse in contrasts; a repeat's source counts as non-repeat; distance ties go to the earlier task",
    "steps are on 100-sample rolling online accuracy, floor 100; an event is censored if the repeat or either comparator misses 0.75; censored tasks count as task length and stay in, which shrinks differences toward 0",
    "accuracy at the end of a source task is its last 100-sample rolling online accuracy",
    "Stage 0 checks without 'all 3 seeds' in the preregistration use the mean over seeds",
    "probe AUC quarters are by task index: first quarter task < 25, last quarter task >= 75, which holds 2 and 3 of the 10 probes; the verdict's probe AUC is the mean of all 10, as in H2",
    "the retry multiplies every condition's tuned rate by 3 and reruns all of Stage 0's conditions; after a retry pass the full run does the same (Deviation 2)",
    "a retry is allowed only when every failed check is plasticity or tension",
    "Stage 0 has its own image pool, so it shares images with neither tuning nor evaluation",
    "both_perm tunes over both_util's candidates; the primary contrast is at both_util's config, its own best is a sensitivity block, as in H2",
    "retention in verdicts averages short and long gaps, as in H2; the manipulation check is either retention measure with a plain 95% CI, as in H2",
    "Holm intervals: step-down percentile intervals, level 0.025 for the smaller bootstrap p, then 0.05 only if the first excludes 0; p = 2 min(P(b<=0), P(b>=0))",
    "noise and ties use numpy's generator, keyed by seed, condition and task; tied order is independent of which SIMD sort a CPU dispatches, but floating point can still differ between CPUs"
  ],
